WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.102
-Our next guest is a very
talented actor and writer

00:00:03.102 --> 00:00:04.671
who received four
Emmy nominations this year

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:06.872
for his work on the hit series
"Ted Lasso,"

00:00:06.872 --> 00:00:09.609
including Best Supporting Actor
in a Comedy Series.

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:11.610
New episodes of "Ted Lasso"

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:14.013
are released Fridays
on Apple TV+.

00:00:14.013 --> 00:00:17.483
Let's take a look.
-Well, that was interesting.

00:00:17.483 --> 00:00:19.151
-Oh, thank you, Doc. Yeah.

00:00:19.151 --> 00:00:21.821
A little something we came up
with back in Kansas.

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:22.989
See, what we're doing is --

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:24.824
-You pretend
to be an ass [bleep]

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:27.694
so the team make you their
common enemy and not Jamie.

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:29.028
-Yeah.
-Oh, yeah.

00:00:29.028 --> 00:00:30.496
-Spot on.
-Got it right away.

00:00:30.496 --> 00:00:32.498
-Mm-hmm.
-Has it ever worked?

00:00:32.498 --> 00:00:33.666
-Uh...
-Uh...

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:35.534
-Tryin 'to remember.
-Uhh, chuck E. Cheese.

00:00:35.534 --> 00:00:37.403
-Chuck E. Cheese.
That's right. Yeah.

00:00:37.403 --> 00:00:40.173
We were at an arcade/pizza joint
in Lincoln, Nebraska

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:41.807
and one of our offensive linemen

00:00:41.807 --> 00:00:43.376
got his head stuck
in a VR machine.

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:45.911
Ended up getting the entire meal
and all our beverages comped

00:00:45.911 --> 00:00:49.048
for free, so...

00:00:49.048 --> 00:00:50.517
-Maybe they don't have
chuck E. Cheese here.

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:52.452
-Oh, yeah. You all might call it
something different here like

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:56.222
Charles Edgar Cheeserton III
or something, right?

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:58.090
-Please welcome back
to the show

00:00:58.090 --> 00:00:59.792
our very good friend
Brendan Hunt.

00:00:59.792 --> 00:01:02.161
How are you, Brendo?
-I'm good.

00:01:02.161 --> 00:01:03.529
How are you?
-I'm wonderful.

00:01:03.529 --> 00:01:06.666
-I'm actually a little annoyed,
Seth, because I was --

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:08.567
I was willing to fly
to New York.

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:10.636
I would have jumped
right on a plane.

00:01:10.636 --> 00:01:12.739
I was told you weren't
having people in the studio!

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:14.074
-Yeah.

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:15.542
-And then old yellow dress
comes out,

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:17.109
and I'm an ass [bleep]
here in my house.

00:01:17.109 --> 00:01:18.611
-Yeah, and it gets worse

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:21.047
because our next guest
is also in studio.

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:23.850
-[ Screams ]

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.686
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:30.757
-Now, to be fair,
I took it upon myself

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:35.360
to not ask that of you
because you are a new dad.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:37.063
Congratulations, Brendan.

00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:38.565
There's your little guy.

00:01:38.565 --> 00:01:41.868
Right away, you're force-feeding
Arsenal into his blood stream.

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:43.169
How is he -- How is he taking

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:46.406
to watching football matches
with you?

00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:48.441
-Oddly enough,
he really seems to like it.

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:52.112
I guess because it's just
a giant sea of green

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:54.346
and, you know,
the only thing that Daddy

00:01:54.346 --> 00:01:56.215
actually cares about,

00:01:56.215 --> 00:01:58.418
so maybe that draws him in
a little bit.

00:01:58.418 --> 00:02:00.086
But he has now watched
more soccer games

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:01.654
at the age of almost 7 months

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:03.789
than I had by the time
I was 26 years old.

00:02:03.789 --> 00:02:06.959
-Yes. You came to it --
You came to it very late.

00:02:06.959 --> 00:02:09.795
I watched a game
with my 5- and 3-year-old,

00:02:09.795 --> 00:02:12.832
and I thought they would
be excited for it.

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:15.734
And the only thing they liked
was when a player got hurt,

00:02:15.734 --> 00:02:19.873
and the doctors ran out
and sprayed their ankles.

00:02:19.873 --> 00:02:21.507
They thought it was amazing

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:23.910
that there were just, like,
doctors on the scene.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:27.613
-"They're cleaning him, Daddy."
-"They're cleaning him up."

00:02:27.613 --> 00:02:29.848
So, 20 nominations
for "Ted Lasso."

00:02:29.848 --> 00:02:34.286
This is a show you both star in,
write on, created.

00:02:34.286 --> 00:02:38.724
And morning of, I mean,
you guys I think probably

00:02:38.724 --> 00:02:40.827
had some hope that there
would be some nominations.

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:42.629
You couldn't have imagined
it would be 20.

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:45.230
How did you find out the news?
-Well, yeah.

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:47.599
I mean, we had done all right
in the previous ones,

00:02:47.599 --> 00:02:48.801
you know, this season,

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:51.437
so like, "Yeah, we'll
probably get one or two."

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:53.005
But I was hoping
to sleep through it

00:02:53.005 --> 00:02:55.008
because then I don't
have to worry about nothin'.

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:58.477
And, again, I have...
at that time.

00:02:58.477 --> 00:03:01.113
So he had other plans.

00:03:01.113 --> 00:03:03.983
So at that point I'm having my
Cheerios and keeping him alive.

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:05.785
It was just like,
"All right. I'll turn it on."

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:07.920
And...yeah.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:10.389
Then, you know, we got nominated
and Jason gets nominated,

00:03:10.389 --> 00:03:12.125
and then, like,
the show's over.

00:03:12.125 --> 00:03:13.526
Like, "Oh. Okay.

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:15.328
I thought there were usually
more categories, but all right."

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:18.230
And I didn't know that they were
only showing part of them.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:21.567
So then my manager is calling me
with like, you know --

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:25.204
as if he was on, like, a rocket
skateboard of some kind.

00:03:25.204 --> 00:03:26.772
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:26.772 --> 00:03:28.674
-[ Shouting gibberish ]

00:03:28.674 --> 00:03:31.377
And all these things.
So...yeah.

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:32.945
It was an all right
little morning.

00:03:32.945 --> 00:03:34.914
I'm just so happy so many people
from the show

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:37.716
got nominated, though,
like, you know, down into

00:03:37.716 --> 00:03:39.552
the "creative art" categories
and everything.

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:40.953
That was cool.
-It was great.

00:03:40.953 --> 00:03:42.955
You know, we talked to your
co-star, Hannah, this week.

00:03:42.955 --> 00:03:45.358
I should say last week.

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:48.160
And she was saying that you
guys are as close as it seems,

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:50.797
and one of the really cool
things in a category

00:03:50.797 --> 00:03:54.400
with eight nominees
that you're in,

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.836
three of the other seven
are your co-stars.

00:03:56.836 --> 00:04:00.038
It just must be
such a cool feeling.

00:04:00.038 --> 00:04:02.575
-Yeah.
I mean, it's -- it's --

00:04:02.575 --> 00:04:05.177
But it's already ruined our
relationships with each other.

00:04:05.177 --> 00:04:06.645
-Sure.
Well, I was gonna say.

00:04:06.645 --> 00:04:08.414
I mean, I know
from our friendship,

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:11.584
I know you to be
a really petty person.

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:13.019
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:15.121
I mean, as soon as you started
getting nominated for Emmys,

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:16.822
even though I wasn't on
any TV shows,

00:04:16.822 --> 00:04:18.490
I was just like, "What, him?!"

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:19.825
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:19.825 --> 00:04:21.360
And I carry that with me
to this day.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:22.761
It's gotten me so far.

00:04:22.761 --> 00:04:24.863
-You would text and say,
"I thought this was my year."

00:04:24.863 --> 00:04:28.334
And I'd say, "Brendan, you're
not on a television show."

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:30.436
-Ugh. You and your dumb reality.

00:04:30.436 --> 00:04:33.339
Dump on my dreams.

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:35.774
-Hey, this --
So, again, you know,

00:04:35.774 --> 00:04:37.876
I was sort of present
at creation,

00:04:37.876 --> 00:04:42.448
not of "Ted Lasso" but of
when you became a soccer fan.

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:44.149
Because I was just like you.

00:04:44.149 --> 00:04:46.452
And it wasn't until we lived
together in Amsterdam

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:48.921
that I think we realized
what a beautiful game it was.

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:50.522
But this really is special.

00:04:50.522 --> 00:04:53.693
You got to be
one of the falconers

00:04:53.693 --> 00:04:56.562
for a game in L.A.

00:04:56.562 --> 00:05:01.000
Tell me about what the role
of the falconer is at this game

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:04.771
and why this team has falcons.

00:05:04.771 --> 00:05:06.972
-I wish I could tell you why.
-Sure.

00:05:06.972 --> 00:05:09.508
-That part, really,
I guess because --

00:05:09.508 --> 00:05:10.676
Oh, I just figured it out.

00:05:10.676 --> 00:05:12.578
Because if you mix up
the letters of LAFC,

00:05:12.578 --> 00:05:15.414
you have two-thirds of "falcon."

00:05:15.414 --> 00:05:17.015
-[ Fingers snap ]
-Boom. Great.

00:05:17.015 --> 00:05:19.451
So now we know that one.
But, yeah.

00:05:19.451 --> 00:05:22.755
It's like the ceremonial
pregame first pitch, basically.

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:25.124
It's, like --
They have this falcon.

00:05:25.124 --> 00:05:27.093
And someone releases it,
and it flies around,

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:28.294
and it catches a little chip

00:05:28.294 --> 00:05:30.296
that has the logo
of the opposing team,

00:05:30.296 --> 00:05:33.099
and the falcon tears that
to bits.

00:05:33.099 --> 00:05:34.534
What you don't know
until you do it --

00:05:34.534 --> 00:05:36.002
And, you know, great honor.

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:39.538
I was so happy to do it.
I had seen it happen many times.

00:05:39.538 --> 00:05:41.941
You have there in your hand
a picture of me being pooped on.

00:05:41.941 --> 00:05:43.709
That is the exact moment...
-Really?

00:05:43.709 --> 00:05:45.611
-...the falcon is poop--
You can't see it

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:47.680
because of the J.J. Abrams flair

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:49.415
coming out
of the falcon's butthole.

00:05:49.415 --> 00:05:51.617
-Right. That's why
they put that light there.

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:54.920
-Probably. Probably.
They know what's up.

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:56.555
Yeah, and I, like,
wiped it on my back,

00:05:56.555 --> 00:05:58.290
and I didn't know
that it was on my back,

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:01.327
and so I had falcon poop
for the entirety of that game,

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:04.129
which was also
a humbling 4-1 home loss.

00:06:04.129 --> 00:06:05.364
-Oh, man.
-So I'm a good-luck charm

00:06:05.364 --> 00:06:07.066
for LAFC, and I'm very proud.

00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:09.735
-It is -- It's kind of nicer
than a first pitch, though,

00:06:09.735 --> 00:06:12.037
because a first pitch
you can really reveal

00:06:12.037 --> 00:06:13.706
that maybe you're bad
at a sport.

00:06:13.706 --> 00:06:16.809
But nobody is gonna say like,
"Oh, that's his first falcon."

00:06:16.809 --> 00:06:19.011
[ Laughter ]

00:06:19.011 --> 00:06:20.313
You -- This is --

00:06:20.313 --> 00:06:22.080
We were talking
about this recently

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:24.750
because Amber Ruffin,
who also worked with us

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:27.953
at Boom Chicago,
was wearing a blond wig recently

00:06:27.953 --> 00:06:32.157
and speaking in sort of a --
a broken European accent.

00:06:32.157 --> 00:06:35.294
And I was like, "Oh, you're
doing Uda from Boom Chicago.

00:06:35.294 --> 00:06:37.263
This was a sketch
that you used to do

00:06:37.263 --> 00:06:41.934
with Oscar winner
Jordan Peele at Boom Chicago.

00:06:41.934 --> 00:06:43.502
There you are.
You're playing Bono.

00:06:43.502 --> 00:06:47.806
And there is our friend
Jordan Peele.

00:06:47.806 --> 00:06:51.710
Is it weird now to look back at
your time living in Amsterdam?

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:53.780
Or do you just have
fond memories?

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:56.114
-Oh, gosh. Only fond memories.
You know?

00:06:56.114 --> 00:06:58.150
I mean, but it's fun.

00:06:58.150 --> 00:07:00.386
Like, we had, you know,
crazy partying times there

00:07:00.386 --> 00:07:02.121
on top of getting our chops up

00:07:02.121 --> 00:07:04.657
doing constant performing
for drunk people.

00:07:04.657 --> 00:07:07.059
-Talking -- Speaking of,
you talk about crazy times,

00:07:07.059 --> 00:07:08.928
and I want to make sure
we get to this.

00:07:08.928 --> 00:07:11.463
Talk about the Gonzo parties
you used to do

00:07:11.463 --> 00:07:13.165
and the role you played in them

00:07:13.165 --> 00:07:15.867
and how much worse it would have
been if cellphones were around.

00:07:15.867 --> 00:07:18.437
[ Laughter ]
-Well, yeah.

00:07:18.437 --> 00:07:22.374
There were these parties that
were hosted by Australian Dave,

00:07:22.374 --> 00:07:24.043
and they were full-on

00:07:24.043 --> 00:07:25.844
just "wear whatever the hell
you want" costume parties.

00:07:25.844 --> 00:07:27.713
Like, not themed.
Just go for it.

00:07:27.713 --> 00:07:30.482
And so I would literally just
dig through a pile of clothes

00:07:30.482 --> 00:07:33.552
and put on crazy stuff and --

00:07:33.552 --> 00:07:38.357
Yeah, I often think about, like,
the fun that kids have today

00:07:38.357 --> 00:07:40.526
has just got to be ruined
and curtailed by the notion

00:07:40.526 --> 00:07:42.394
that you're gonna be online
at any moment.

00:07:42.394 --> 00:07:43.796
We did not have that.

00:07:43.796 --> 00:07:45.931
I feel like maybe we were
the last chunk of people

00:07:45.931 --> 00:07:48.935
having ridiculous behavior
out in public

00:07:48.935 --> 00:07:50.903
that we'll never have
that chance again

00:07:50.903 --> 00:07:52.472
without fear of repercussion.

00:07:52.472 --> 00:07:55.574
And we've lost
something there, Seth.

00:07:55.574 --> 00:07:59.812
"Back in my day, we would
have to walk to school. Ooh."

00:07:59.812 --> 00:08:01.313
-I like that if you went --

00:08:01.313 --> 00:08:03.415
If you said, "My friend Dave's
hosting a party,"

00:08:03.415 --> 00:08:05.150
you'd say, "Oh, that's
probably a normal party."

00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:07.519
But if you said, "Australian
Dave is hosting a party,"

00:08:07.519 --> 00:08:11.957
it'd be like, "Oh [bleep].
I hope there aren't cameras!"

00:08:11.957 --> 00:08:15.327
Hey, buddy, congratulations
on all your nominations.

00:08:15.327 --> 00:08:18.097
You're nominated a couple times
for writing, as well,

00:08:18.097 --> 00:08:20.132
which are also so well-deserved.
And thank you.

00:08:20.132 --> 00:08:21.767
It's always great
to see your face.

00:08:21.767 --> 00:08:23.569
-Great to see you.
Thanks for having me.

00:08:23.569 --> 00:08:25.270
-"Ted Lasso"
is streaming on Apple TV+

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:27.072
with new episodes released
every Friday.

00:08:27.072 --> 00:08:28.875
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

